.TH AVR\-REPO\-MIRROR\-CREATE 1 "" "avr 0.4.1" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-repo-mirror-create \- Enable mirroring and place a connected repository at a location.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr repo mirror create
[OPTIONS] REPOSITORY
.SH DESCRIPTION
Enable mirroring and place a connected repository at a location.
.PP
REPOSITORY is an owner/repo name on GitHub or a namespace/repo name on GitLab (including nested groups). It must already be connected to the selected Avrea organization. Requires the organization admin role.
.PP
Safe to repeat: existing placements and their source configuration are preserved. The initial sync runs asynchronously; use `mirror status` with the returned repository ID to check progress.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr repo mirror locations
    avr repo mirror create acme/widgets --location gsc-fi
    avr repo mirror create acme/team/widgets --source gitlab --location gsc-fi
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    enabled, full_name, placements, repository_id
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIREPOSITORY\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Source hosting the repository. (choices: github, gitlab; default: github)
.TP
\fB\-\-location\fR \fITEXT\fR
Cluster ID, datacenter ID, or unique name from `avr repo mirror locations`. (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses the default organization.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
